' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' --- The document engine ---
'
' Most of the public surface is free functions over plain structs, which the
' automated pass cannot show: load_data, parse_market_data, parse_fixings,
' parse_ore_log and roundtrip. Only the mappers, the importer, the exporter,
' the planner, the scanner and the generated entity stack are classes.

' trade_mapper dispatches one ORE trade to the instrument mapper that owns its
' asset class. Each instrument mapper carries a forward_* and a reverse_* pair
' per trade type it handles.
ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper ..> ores::ore::domain::swap_instrument_mapper : dispatches
ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper ..> ores::ore::domain::fx_instrument_mapper : dispatches
ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper ..> ores::ore::domain::credit_instrument_mapper : dispatches
ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper ..> ores::ore::domain::bond_instrument_mapper : dispatches
ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper ..> ores::ore::domain::equity_instrument_mapper : dispatches
ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper ..> ores::ore::domain::commodity_instrument_mapper : dispatches
ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper ..> ores::ore::domain::scripted_instrument_mapper : dispatches
ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper ..> ores::ore::domain::composite_instrument_mapper : dispatches

' The importer reads four document kinds; the exporter writes all four. The
' exporter reaches the instrument mappers as well as the document mappers,
' because it serialises any trade the importer produced.
ores::ore::xml::importer --> ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper : uses
ores::ore::xml::importer --> ores::ore::domain::conventions_mapper : uses
ores::ore::xml::importer --> ores::ore::domain::currency_mapper : uses
ores::ore::xml::importer --> ores::ore::domain::calendar_adjustment_mapper : uses
ores::ore::xml::exporter --> ores::ore::domain::trade_mapper : uses
ores::ore::xml::exporter --> ores::ore::domain::conventions_mapper : uses
ores::ore::xml::exporter --> ores::ore::domain::currency_mapper : uses
ores::ore::xml::exporter --> ores::ore::domain::calendar_adjustment_mapper : uses

' roundtrip is a free function, so it has no class to hang off. It composes
' the importer and the exporter over one directory and owns neither; it is the
' only thing in the component that writes to disk.
note right of "ores::ore::xml::roundtrip_summary"
    Produced by xml::roundtrip(in, out), a free function that composes
    the importer and the exporter. It walks a directory, re-exports
    what it read, and records every document it could not carry. The
    count is split into unsupported kinds, which the importer does not
    handle, and failed kinds, whose re-read did not match; each failure
    keeps its path and its message.
end note

' --- The import planner ---
'
' The planner decides what an import will do before anything is written. It
' builds the portfolio and book hierarchy from what the scan found, and reads
' trades through the importer rather than the scanner, so that a file it
' cannot parse is reported rather than silently skipped.
ores::ore::planner::ore_import_planner --> ores::ore::hierarchy::ore_hierarchy_builder : uses
ores::ore::planner::ore_import_planner --> ores::ore::xml::importer : uses

' --- The classifier split ---
'
' Both classifiers ask one root-element reader. Parsing the root element is
' what keeps them honest: a substring match over the first bytes misses a
' root element that carries attributes, matches a keyword inside a comment,
' and can rewrite a curve configuration as an empty conventions document.
ores::ore::scanner::ore_directory_scanner ..> ores::ore::xml::document_kind : classifies by

' --- The market facet ---

' The parsers are free functions, so they have no class to hang off:
' parse_market_data and parse_fixings both take an istream, return
' market_datum, and report each problem through parse_report. Both resolve
' every key through the registry, which is built once from the entity rows.
note right of "ores::ore::market::series_key_registry"
    Built once at construction from the series key shape rows. Every
    market data key is decomposed and resolved through it, so an
    unknown key becomes a parse issue rather than an exception.
end note

' --- The generated entity stack ---

ores::ore::service::series_key_shape_service o-- ores::ore::repository::series_key_shape_repository : owns
ores::ore::repository::series_key_shape_repository ..> ores::ore::repository::series_key_shape_mapper : uses
ores::ore::repository::series_key_shape_mapper --> ores::ore::repository::series_key_shape_entity : maps
ores::ore::messaging::series_key_shape_handler ..> ores::ore::service::series_key_shape_service : uses

